<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann shares under heavy pressure.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann shares under heavy pressure.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German engineering group Mannesmann AG came under heavy selling pressure on Friday as dealers said a well-respected investment research house had downgraded the stock.</p>
<p>Mannesmann shares were down 31.50 marks, or 4.8 percent, at 620.50 marks at 1030 GMT, while the DAX index was down 0.7 percent at 3,325.32 points.</p>
<p>Dealers said Mannesmann had been removed from the buy list by a German bank. No confirmation was immediately available.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
